   "etymology": "Uncertain: Possibly:\n* From Proto-Indo-European *megʰ- (“to be able”), though there's no evidence supporting the fall of the velar.\n* A nasal-infixed formation from the root *mewd- (“to rejoice”), whence also mudà (“possibility”), mudúoti (“to try, attempt”) and Sanskrit मुद् (mud, “to be happy, rejoice”).\n* From Proto-Indo-European *men(s)dʰh₁- (“to pay attention, wisdom”).\n* Akin to Lithuanian išminti̇̀s (“to be able”), išmėginti (“try”), išminti̇̀s (“wisdom”).",
